<task id="021" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-20 ComposeEditBatch (4-phase pipeline)</title>
    <phase>2 LLM Editing Patterns</phase>
    <gate>green</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>phase2-llm</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>003</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>high</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build `ComposeEditBatch` — the deterministic 4-phase pipeline that applies a set of validated edits to a
    document without offset drift. This is the adeu "4-phase atomic batch pipeline" pattern (design §6.1):
    resolve → sort descending → skip overlap → apply bottom-up. Applying bottom-up means earlier (higher-offset)
    edits do not shift the offsets of later (lower-offset) edits, so a multi-edit batch applies cleanly in one pass.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET developer with a bias for pure, deterministic, thoroughly-tested text-transformation code and
    numbered edge-case comments (`// EDGE-N:` per design §6.1).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `ComposeEditBatch` service in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/` that consumes resolved matches
    from `IComposeEditValidator` (FR-19), applies edits via resolve → sort-descending → skip-overlap → apply-bottom-up,
    and returns the transformed document plus an applied/skipped report. Full unit coverage of the closed acceptance set,
    build green, publish size measured.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-20 sits on top of FR-19's validator: the validator resolves and detects overlap; the batch pipeline orders and
      applies. Spike 3 (task 003) validated the 4-phase pipeline + rollback atomicity; its notes are the reference approach.
      FR-21 (ComposeEditTransaction) wraps this batch with snapshot/rollback — keep the batch itself free of transaction
      concerns so FR-21 can compose cleanly.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file change="create">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeEditBatch.cs</file>
      <file change="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeEditModels.cs (extend with batch result types if needed)</file>
      <file change="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/IComposeEditValidator.cs (FR-19 — resolved-match input)</file>
      <file change="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/spikes/ (Spike 3 output — 4-phase pipeline + rollback atomicity)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Spike 3 — atomic edit batch + rollback (informs pipeline + atomicity).</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">FR-19 IComposeEditValidator — provides resolved matches consumed by the batch.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Services/Compose/ MUST NOT inject any AI internal (`IOpenAiClient`/executor/`IConsumerRoutingService`). The batch is pure deterministic text logic.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">DI minimalism — internal pipeline helpers need not be DI-registered; register only what an endpoint or FR-21 requires.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Integration-heavy pyramid; NO banned test shapes (`Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, ctor null-check). Test through the public batch contract with real multi-edit inputs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF publish size ≤ 60 MB compressed (NFR-01); measure and report delta.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>deterministic multi-edit application; offset-stable bottom-up apply; overlap skipping</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="4-phase atomic batch pipeline" location="design.md §6.1">resolve → sort descending → skip overlap → apply bottom-up so earlier edits don't shift later offsets.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    NEW service `ComposeEditBatch`. (1) Existing — no batch application exists; FR-19's validator resolves/validates but
    does not apply. (2) Extension — kept separate from the validator (single-responsibility) and from FR-21's transaction
    wrapper so both can consume it. (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing — applying multiple edits naively (top-down, unsorted) shifts
    every subsequent offset and corrupts the document; without the bottom-up pipeline, multi-edit batches silently drift.
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Context check. Load ADRs/constraints. Read Spike 3 notes for the locked pipeline shape.</step>
    <step order="1">Define/extend batch result types in ComposeEditModels.cs (applied edits, skipped-for-overlap edits, final text).</step>
    <step order="2">Implement `ComposeEditBatch.Apply`: resolve (via FR-19 results) → sort resolved spans descending by start offset → skip edits whose span overlaps an already-accepted higher-offset edit → apply each replacement bottom-up.</step>
    <step order="3">Cover edge cases with `// EDGE-N:` comments: adjacent-but-not-overlapping edits, identical target spans, zero-length insertions, edit at document start/end.</step>
    <step order="4">Register in DI only if consumed directly by an endpoint; otherwise expose for FR-21 to wrap.</step>
    <step order="5">Write unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ComposeEditBatchTests.cs` covering the closed acceptance set.</step>
    <step order="6">Build; run tests; measure + report publish size delta.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeEditBatch.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ComposeEditBatchTests.cs</output>
    <output type="report">Task completion report incl. publish-size delta</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A batch of 3+ non-overlapping edits at different offsets applies with every replacement landing at its correct span (NO offset drift) — verified by asserting the exact transformed text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Edits are applied bottom-up (descending start offset) so an earlier-in-document edit's length change does not shift a later edit's resolved offset.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Two edits whose resolved spans overlap: the pipeline skips one and reports it in the skipped list rather than corrupting the text (NEGATIVE: overlap).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An empty edit list returns the document unchanged; a zero-length insertion applies at the correct offset (NEGATIVE: empty batch / degenerate span).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The batch returns a report distinguishing applied vs skipped edits; `ComposeEditBatch` injects zero AI internals; `dotnet build` green; publish size ≤ 60 MB reported with delta.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
